      "updated": 1784655825375,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- \"Fundamentals of Data Engineering\" — Joe Reis & Matt Housley (O'Reilly) — the modern go-to book on the discipline's lifecycle and \"undercurrents.\"\n- \"Designing Data-Intensive Applications\" — Martin Kleppmann (O'Reilly) — canonical deep-dive on distributed systems, consistency, and storage engines underlying every data platform.\n- roadmap.sh/data-engineer — community-maintained, visual step-by-step data engineering learning roadmap.\n- Apache Airflow official documentation (airflow.apache.org/docs) — canonical reference for DAG authoring, scheduling, and orchestration best practices.\n- dbt Labs official docs & \"dbt Fundamentals\" course (docs.getdbt.com) — the standard reference for analytics engineering, testing, and data modeling in the modern stack.\n- \"Kafka: The Definitive Guide\" (O'Reilly, Narkhede/Shapira/Palino) plus Confluent's official Kafka docs — canonical resource for streaming semantics and delivery guarantees.\n- The Data Engineering Podcast (dataengineeringpodcast.com) — long-running, well-regarded interview series covering real-world pipeline and orchestration decisions.\n- Awesome Data Engineering (github.com/igorbarinov/awesome-data-engineering) — widely-starred curated GitHub list of tools, papers, and blogs.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- \"Fundamentals of Data Engineering\" — Joe Reis & Matt Housley (O'Reilly) — the modern go-to book on the discipline's lifecycle and \"undercurrents.\"\n- \"Designing Data-Intensive Applications\" — Martin Kleppmann (O'Reilly) — canonical deep-dive on distributed systems, consistency, and storage engines underlying every data platform.\n- roadmap.sh/data-engineer — community-maintained, visual step-by-step data engineering learning roadmap.\n- Apache Airflow official documentation (airflow.apache.org/docs) — canonical reference for DAG authoring, scheduling, and orchestration best practices.\n- dbt Labs official docs & \"dbt Fundamentals\" course (docs.getdbt.com) — the standard reference for analytics engineering, testing, and data modeling in the modern stack.\n- \"Kafka: The Definitive Guide\" (O'Reilly, Narkhede/Shapira/Palino) plus Confluent's official Kafka docs — canonical resource for streaming semantics and delivery guarantees.\n- The Data Engineering Podcast (dataengineeringpodcast.com) — long-running, well-regarded interview series covering real-world pipeline and orchestration decisions.\n- Awesome Data Engineering (github.com/igorbarinov/awesome-data-engineering) — widely-starred curated GitHub list of tools, papers, and blogs.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
